system ordering violation: ['account_service', 'support_platform', 'security_service', 'support_platform', 'integration_service', 'backup_service']\r\n\nLog: file:///C:/Users/Pavan/.gemini/antigravity/brain/51374649-1a7b-432a-985e-98e8fd1f22c3/.system_generated/tasks/task-1440.log\n</SYSTEM_MESSAGE>"}
{"step_index":1444,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-24T21:20:42Z","input_tokens":2204,"cache_read_tokens":208642,"output_tokens":1994,"thinking":"The audit reveals the complete resolution of the initial 22 issues, including the \"INCOMPLETE\" case. A new, isolated issue regarding verification system ordering has emerged. This new issue likely stems from the previous step which sorted steps by an internal dependency key.\n\n\nThe `VERIFICATION` phase's sorting in the step builder requires the `SYSTEM_ORDER` to take precedence. The existing sort key prioritizes the phase order and operation order; therefore, it requires a modification to insert `SYSTEM_ORDER` at the top. The concern about prior tests passing needs to be re-evaluated by comparing the sort against the expected system order, and it's essential to ensure consistency in ordering for valid results.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"import csv\nimport json\n\nSYSTEM_ORDER = {\n    \"account_service\": 1,\n    \"search_service\": 2,\n    \"security_service\": 3,\n    \"support_platform\": 4,\n    \"identity_service\": 5,\n    \"analytics_platform\": 6,\n    \"integration_service\": 7,\n    \"backup_service\": 8,\n    \"export_service\": 9\n}\n\nOP_ORDER = {\n    # FINDING\n    \"REPORT_REMAINING_RECORD\": 0,\n    \"REPORT_EXPOSED_PII\": 1,\n    \"REPORT_ACTIVE_DATA_FLOW\": 2,\n    \"REPORT_RESTORE_RISK\": 3,\n    # REMEDIATION\n    \"DISABLE_DATA_FLOW\": 0,\n    \"DISABLE_FLOW\": 0,\n    \"BLOCK_RESTORE\": 1,\n    \"DELETE_RECORD\": 2,\n    \"REDACT_RECORD\": 3,\n    \"ANONYMIZE_RECORD\": 4,\n    # VERIFICATION\n    \"VERIFY_RECORD_ABSENT\": 0,\n    \"VERIFY_RECORD_PRESENT\": 1,\n    \"VERIFY_RECORD_REDACTED\": 2,\n    \"VERIFY_RECORD_ANONYMIZED\": 3,\n    \"VERIFY_DATA_FLOW_DISABLED\": 4,\n    \"VERIFY_FLOW_DISABLED\": 4,\n    \"VERIFY_RESTORE_BLOCKED\": 5,\n    \"VERIFY_TOMBSTONE_CREATED\": 6,\n}\n\nwith open(\"dataset/sample_output.csv\", encoding=\"utf-8-sig\") as f:\n    expected = {r[\"case_id\"]: json.loads(r[\"steps_json\"]) for r in csv.DictReader(f)}\n\n# Test both sort keys on sample_output\npassed_A = 0\npassed_B = 0\n\nfor cid, steps in expected.items():\n    # Sort A: step 871 key (PHASE, OP_ORDER, system_id, resource_id)\n    sorted_A = sorted(steps, key=lambda s: (\n        {\"FINDING\": 0, \"REMEDIATION\": 1, \"VERIFICATION\": 2}[s[\"phase\"]],\n        OP_ORDER.get(s[\"operation\"], 99),\n        s[\"system_id\"],\n        s[\"resource_id\"]\n    ))\n    for i, s in enumerate(sorted_A, 1):\n        s[\"step_no\"] = i\n    if sorted_A == steps:\n        passed_A += 1\n\n    # Sort B: (PHASE, SYSTEM_ORDER for verif)\n    sorted_B = sorted(steps, key=lambda s: (\n        {\"FINDING\": 0, \"REMEDIATION\": 1, \"VERIFICATION\": 2}[s[\"phase\"]],\n        SYSTEM_ORDER.get(s[\"system_id\"], 99) if s[\"phase\"] == \"VERIFICATION\" else OP_ORDER.get(s[\"operation\"], 99),\n        OP_ORDER.get(s[\"operation\"], 99),\n        s[\"resource_id\"]\n    ))\n    for i, s in enumerate(sorted_B, 1):\n        s[\"step_no\"] = i\n    if sorted_B == steps:\n        passed_B += 1\n\nprint(f\"Sort A passed on sample_output: {passed_A}/32\")\nprint(f\"Sort B passed on sample_output: {passed_B}/32\")\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:/Users/Pavan/hackerrank-orchestrate-october26/test_sort_keys.py"}}]}
